title: 'Anthropic, "Building effective agents" (2024): start with the simplest thing, and add steps only when they demonstrably improve the outcome.'
pid: 272c2776-82fa-41cf-aba2-a0aeb7e53cc3
body: |2-
  https://www.anthropic.com/engineering/building-effective-agents
  The workflows it names fit us: our process is prompt chaining with
  gates (plan, read, build, check) and an orchestrator (Top). Agents
  should pause for human input "at checkpoints or when encountering
  blockers", and have stopping conditions. Its three principles:
  simplicity, transparency of the plan, careful interfaces.
